From 4714c15011d2de9961026d2be8c9a7a55344d60d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yi Xie <imxieyi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 30 Aug 2026 01:55:46 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] arm64: add a dedicated x86-64 userspace UML slice

Keep the UML kernel and kernel-mode execution arm64 while making the
dedicated 4 KiB Darwin compatibility slice accept only EM_X86_64
userspace. Expose fixed x86-64 ELF, ptrace, core-register, TLS, syscall,
and signal semantics without per-task architecture selection.

Route native x86-64 and long-mode INT 0x80 entries through the gadget
syscall adapters and construct native x86-64 signal and XSAVE frames.
Add the slice-scoped MAP_32BIT and MAP_ABOVE4G flags plus low-window and
above-4-GiB unmapped-area allocation.

Leave the shared host/kernel ABI, the native arm64 slice, and Android
unchanged. Syscalls whose compat argument layouts require explicit
adapters remain rejected.

Signed-off-by: Yi Xie <imxieyi@users.noreply.github.com>
